warning[NK1308]: `p` reaches the path `fs::read_to_string` opens under `fs::Root::Anywhere`, which may name any file, and it comes from outside the program.
= help: Open it under a root the program chose, where it cannot leave the directory: `fs::Root::Dir(".")`, `fs::scratch()` or `root.join(...)` of one. Or check it where it arrives, `throw BadInput(p) if !path::is_component(p)` (or `path::is_below`), and open it under such a root or joined to a part that is not outside. If the program means to read paths from `args`, `untrusted-paths-read = ["args"]` under `[allow]` in the manifest builds it.
